    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d511">

                <pb facs="1037" n="1007" sameAs="frus:frus1947v01/pg1007"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">560.AL/10–647: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Troutman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-10-06T11:00:00+01:00">October 6, 1947—11
                            a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1084. Personal for Wilcox from Brown. Have reached satisfactory agreement Coombs.
                    TAC acts today:<anchor n="1" xml:id="d511-f1"/> Australian Cabinet acts
                    tomorrow. TAC yesterday tentatively agreed recommend agreement UK general basis
                    outlined mytel 1077, October 4.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d511-f2"/> Final decision
                    today. Am well satisfied.</p>
                <p>Having serious difficulty Canada apple preference. Seeing Wilgress again today.
                    [Brown.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Troutman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d511-f1" n="1" xml:id="d511-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram 1088 from Geneva, October 6, not printed, Brown reported that the
                    Trade Agreements Committee “unanimously approved agreement I reached with
                    Coombs.” (560.AL/10–647)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d511-f2" n="2" xml:id="d511-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
